                <pb facs="0494" n="370" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg370"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.48/594: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Atherton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-08-19T16:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 19,
                                1923—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>120. Department’s telegram 51 August 15 [<hi rendition="#italic">18</hi>], 2 p.m.
                    Upon arrival of Director Jaquith Near East Relief I suggested to him that he
                    [apparent omission] conversation with the Minister for Foreign Affairs reported
                    in my cipher telegram 117, August 7, 6 p.m. Jaquith informed me yesterday he has
                    made an arrangement very much as reported in my 117, August 7, 6 p.m. and that
                    he understood two Greek vessels with some of the refugees aboard have already
                    left Constantinople for Saloniki.</p>
                <p>I understand League of Nations will care for some 5,000 of these refugees in
                    [Thrace?]. Constantinople informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atherton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
